# Line endings. Text is stored with LF line endings. The files a test compares output with (approved files) and the
# shell scripts are LF on every machine, whatever a person's core.autocrlf setting, so a test gives the same answer
# on Windows. Windows' own script keeps its CRLF line endings as they are.
* text=auto
*.approved.* text eol=lf
*.received.* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.pl text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat -text
*.m4a binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
